The Internet is a large worldwide network that connects people and devices from different places. We can use it to visit websites, watch videos, use social media, send emails, and much more.

An intranet is a private network used by a particular organization, such as a college or company. For example, in college, if students use the college Wi-Fi to access a private student portal, notices, attendance, or study materials available only to college members, that is an intranet.

For example, when I use college Wi-Fi to open Google or Instagram, I am using the Internet. But when I access a website or portal meant only for students and staff of my college, I am using the intranet.

So, the main difference is that the Internet is available globally, while an intranet is restricted to a specific organization and its authorized users.
